  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRIANGLE in ASEAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tripartite Action to Enhance the Contribution of Labour Migration to Growth and Development in ASEAN project (TRIANGLE in ASEAN) is a 10-year (2015-2025) investment implemented by the International Labour Organization (ILO). It aims to maximise the contribution of labour migration to equitable, inclusive and stable growth in the ASEAN region, and reduce the vulnerability of migrant workers to trafficking.  TRIANGLE works regionally with ASEAN Member States and bodies, and nationally in six target ASEAN countries, to support their efforts to implement the 2007 ASEAN Declaration on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Migrant Workers and the 2017 ASEAN Consensus on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Migrant Workers.</narrative>
  </description>
