  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening regional architecture</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adoption of ASEAN Guideline on the Protection of Migrant Workers in Crisis Situations
&#x200d;
In May 2023, ASEAN leaders mandated the ASEAN Committee on Migrant Workers to develop guidance to implement the ASEAN Declaration on the Protection of Migrant Workers and Family Members in Crisis Situations. The Guideline, which articulates guiding principles on policies, institutional mechanisms, programs, and services, was adopted at the September 2023 ASEAN Summit. This represents a significant advancement in regional protection for migrant workers and their families. 
&#x200d;
Australia&#x2019;s TRIANGLE in ASEAN program ($24 million, 2015-2025) supports safe and fair labour migration in ASEAN.  It supported preparation of these guideline through background papers, facilitating drafting, consultations, and providing technical inputs. The program provided financial and logistical support for consultations in collaboration with partners.  Our support has ensured guidance is consistent with international labour standards and addresses critical issues facing migrant workers during crises.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the launch of a TRIANGLE study on Thai Employment and Working Conditions in the Agriculture Sector (May 2022), the Thai Ministry of Labour (MoL) committed to reviewing its Ministerial Regulation on Labour Protection in Agricultural Work &#x2013; a key instrument ensuring protection of agriculture workers, many of whom are migrant workers. MoL requested TRIANGLE to provide technical support and advice on the review process for the regulation and was invited to be a member of the review committee. In the first meeting (August 2022), the committee agreed to explore the extension of workers&#x2019; entitlements (e.g. minimum wage, overtime provisions).</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
